    introEn: `Founded in 1956, Beijing Tiantan Hospital is a large Grade 3A comprehensive hospital affiliated with Capital Medical University and one of the world's top three neurosurgery research centers. Characterized by neuroscience, the hospital leads internationally in cerebrovascular diseases, neurosurgery, neurointervention, and neurology. It hosts the National Clinical Research Center for Neurological Diseases and the National Neurological Diseases Medical Quality Control Center. Tiantan Hospital has achieved internationally advanced levels in brain aneurysm clipping and embolization, brain AVM treatment, brain tumor microsurgery, and spinal surgery, performing over 10,000 neurosurgeries annually. The hospital hosts top experts including Academicians of the Chinese Academy of Engineering, including Professors Zhao Jizong and Wang Zhongcheng. The new campus, located on the South Fourth Ring Road, covers 200,000 square meters, making it the largest single-building neurological hospital in China.`,
