    introEn: `Founded in 1915, Peking University First Hospital is the first clinical medical college established by Peking University and one of the earliest national hospitals in China. It is a hospital directly managed by the National Health Commission, integrating clinical care, education, research, and prevention, with comprehensive strength ranking among the top nationally. The hospital leads in urology, nephrology, dermatology and venereology, obstetrics and gynecology, and pediatrics. The urology department is the birthplace of Chinese urology and one of the largest urology centers in China. The nephrology department is the National Quality Control Center for Kidney Diseases, with rich experience in chronic kidney disease, renal failure, and kidney transplantation. The hospital hosts multiple national clinical research centers and serves as a national drug clinical trial institution. It is also the First Clinical Medical College of Peking University, undertaking extensive medical education. Annual outpatient visits exceed 3 million.`,
